<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{% comment %}
Rendered by django.contrib.sitemaps.views.sitemap (see urls.py) with
StaticViewSitemap (apps/main/sitemaps.py) as the single source of URLs — this
template intentionally shadows Django's built-in sitemap.xml. Paths come from
StaticViewSitemap.items() via URL reversal, so adding/removing a page there is
all that's needed — do not hand-list URLs here again. The host is pinned to the
canonical non-www domain: every page self-canonicalizes to non-www, and the old
www vs non-www split is what kept /massage/ out of Google's index.
{% endcomment %}<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{% for url in urlset %}    <url>
        <loc>https://acceleratedrehabtherapy.com{% url url.item %}</loc>
        <lastmod>{% now 'Y-m-d' %}</lastmod>
        <changefreq>{{ url.changefreq }}</changefreq>
        <priority>{{ url.priority }}</priority>
    </url>
{% endfor %}</urlset>
